# Crush LSP config (verified against crush 0.88.1 / powernap v0.1.6).
# Managed declaratively in home-manager/modules/tools/crush.nix.

# Crush does NOT need an LSP roster the way helix does. options.auto_lsp
# (default TRUE) matches each file it touches against a bundled registry of
# 365 servers and starts the ones whose command is on PATH. Only the gaps
# need a `lsp` entry.

# WHICH SERVERS THE REGISTRY ALREADY KNOWS (name | command):
#   rust_analyzer | rust-analyzer      nil_ls | nil        nixd | nixd
#   gopls | gopls   golangci_lint_ls | golangci-lint-langserver
#   zls | zls       just | just-lsp    harper_ls | harper-ls
#   kotlin_language_server | kotlin-language-server
#   dartls | dart   sourcekit | sourcekit-lsp   marksman, taplo, bashls, ...
# NOT in it, despite overrides.go naming them: ts_ls, jsonls, html, cssls,
# yamlls, jdtls. Those need explicit entries or the language has no server.

# Dump the whole registry for the pinned crush:
git clone --depth 1 --branch powernap/v0.1.6 https://github.com/charmbracelet/x /tmp/x
jq -r 'to_entries[] | "\(.key)\t\(.value.command)\t\(.value.filetypes // [] | join(","))"' \
  /tmp/x/powernap/pkg/config/lsps.json | column -t

# THREE BEHAVIOURS THAT DECIDE HOW TO WRITE AN ENTRY
# (internal/lsp/manager.go):
#
# 1. An `lsp` entry REPLACES the bundled server, it does not layer onto it
#    (NewManager -> AddServer). Writing `"gopls": {"command": "gopls"}` drops
#    gopls's filetypes and root_markers - and an empty filetypes list means
#    "handles every file". Restate the whole definition or don't touch it.
#
# 2. A user-configured server SKIPS the exec.LookPath check that auto-start
#    does. A bundled server whose binary is missing is silently skipped; a
#    configured one is respawned and fails on every file open. Hence the
#    absolute /nix/store paths in crush.nix rather than bare names.
#
# 3. A user-configured server also skips skipAutoStartCommands - the list of
#    commands too generic to auto-start (dart, java, node, npx, python,
#    deno, dotnet, ruff, ...). Naming `dartls` is the ONLY way to get Dart,
#    even though the registry already defines it correctly.

# Filetype matching is suffix-based ("ts" -> endswith ".ts") OR equal to
# powernap's detected language kind. ".mts" does NOT end with ".ts", so list
# mts/cts/mjs/cjs separately. Root markers are globbed in the WORKING DIR
# only (non-recursive); an empty list means "no project needed".

# Debug what actually started:
#   crushrc:  option debug true; option debug-lsp true
tail -f ~/.local/share/crush/logs/crush.log | grep -i lsp
